    "prompt": "The figure shows the floor plan of Renate's house. Renate enters her house from the porch and walks through each door exactly once. In which room does she end up?",
    "image": "qimages/kangaroo/ca-2018-g1112/q02.webp",
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "1"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "2"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "3"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "4"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "5"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "B",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Count doors per room",
        "body": "From the plan, the doors connect: porch–5, 5–1, 1–2, 2–3, 2–4 and 3–4. So the number of doors is: porch 1, room 5: 2, room 1: 2, room 2: 3, room 3: 2, room 4: 2.\n\nWhenever Renate passes through a room she uses two of its doors (one in, one out). So a room with an odd number of doors can only be the start or the end of her walk. The odd ones are the porch (where she starts) and room 2 — she ends in **room 2**.\n\n**Answer: (B) 2**"
      },
      {
        "title": "Find a route",
        "body": "Porch → 5 → 1 → 2 → 3 → 4 → 2 uses each of the six doors exactly once and ends in room 2.\n\n**Answer: (B) 2**"
      }
    ],
