    "type": "mc",
    "prompt": "The shape shown is made of 12 cubes glued together. The shape is dipped into a bucket of paint covering the surface entirely. How many of the cubes will be painted on exactly four of their faces?",
    "image": "qimages/kangaroo/ca-2018-g1112/q04.webp",
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "11"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "7"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "8"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "9"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "10"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "C",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Count neighbours",
        "body": "A cube is painted on exactly four faces exactly when it is glued to exactly **two** other cubes.\n\nRead the shape: a column of 4 cubes on the left; a front row of 3 more cubes to its right; behind the right-most front cube one more cube, and behind that a back row of 3 cubes (the right-most one carrying one cube on top).\n\nGo along the shape:\n- the top cube of the left column touches 1 cube; the other three cubes of the column touch 2;\n- the 3 front-row cubes and the cube behind the right one touch 2 each;\n- the right cube of the back row touches 3 (the cube in front of it, the cube on top, its left neighbour);\n- the cube on top touches 1; the middle back cube touches 2; the left back cube touches 1.\n\nCubes touching exactly 2 others: $3+4+1 = 8$.\n\n**Answer: (C) 8**"
      },
      {
        "title": "Count gluings",
        "body": "The 12 cubes form a tree (no loops), so there are $11$ gluings, i.e. $22$ glued faces in total. There are three end cubes with 1 neighbour (top of the left column, the cube on top at the back, the left back cube) and one branch cube with 3 neighbours. If $x$ cubes have 2 neighbours, then $3\\cdot1 + 3 + 2x = 22$, so $x=8$.\n\n**Answer: (C) 8**"
      }
    ],
    "topics": [
      "spatial",
      "counting"
    ],
    "difficulty": 1,
