    "timeMinutes": null,
    "type": "mc",
    "prompt": "If $a$ and $b$ are digits and $\\frac ab = b.a$ ($b.a$ is a decimal), find $a+b$.",
    "image": null,
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "7"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "8"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "9"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "10"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "11"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "A",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Turn it into an equation",
        "body": "$b.a = b + \\frac{a}{10}$, so\n$$\\frac ab = b+\\frac a{10} \\;\\Rightarrow\\; 10a = 10b^2 + ab \\;\\Rightarrow\\; a(10-b) = 10b^2.$$\nTry $b=1,\\dots,9$: $a = \\frac{10b^2}{10-b}$ gives $\\frac{10}9, 5, \\frac{90}7, \\frac{160}6, 50, \\dots$ — the only digit is $a=5$ for $b=2$ (larger $b$ give $a\\ge 50$).\n\nCheck: $\\frac52 = 2.5$. ✓ So $a+b=7$.\n\n**Answer: (A) 7**"
      },
      {
        "title": "Guess and check",
        "body": "$b.a$ lies between $b$ and $b+1$, and $\\frac ab\\le\\frac 9b$. So $b\\le \\frac9b$, i.e. $b\\le 3$. $b=1$: $a=1.a$ impossible. $b=2$: $\\frac a2=2.a$ needs $a\\in\\{4,5\\}$; $\\frac52=2.5$ works. $b=3$: $\\frac a3\\ge3$ needs $a=9$, but $3\\ne3.9$.\n\n**Answer: (A) 7**"
      }
    ],
    "topics": [
      "number-theory",
      "fractions-decimals"
    ],
    "difficulty": 1,
    "duplicateOf": null,
    "reviewNote": null
